  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Although this ability triggers when the Incarnation is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, it doesn’t *specifically* trigger on leaving the battlefield, so it doesn’t behave like other leaves-the-battlefield abilities. The ability will trigger from the graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "23ef92b0-2298-4e8d-bf64-46d096c84a9d",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the Incarnation had lost this ability while on the battlefield (due to Lignify, for example) and then was destroyed, the ability would still trigger and it would get shuffled into its owner’s library. However, if the Incarnation lost this ability when it was put into the graveyard (due to Yixlid Jailer, for example), the ability wouldn’t trigger and the Incarnation would remain in the graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "23ef92b0-2298-4e8d-bf64-46d096c84a9d",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the Incarnation is removed from the graveyard after the ability triggers but before it resolves, it will remain in its new zone when its owner shuffles their library. Similarly, if a replacement effect has the Incarnation move to a different zone instead of being put into the graveyard, the ability won’t trigger at all.",
      "oracle_id": "23ef92b0-2298-4e8d-bf64-46d096c84a9d",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The last ability triggers when the Incarnation is put into its owner’s graveyard from any zone, not just from on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "23ef92b0-2298-4e8d-bf64-46d096c84a9d",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect says to set a player's life total to a number that's higher than the player's current life total while Giant Cindermaw is on the battlefield, the player's life total doesn't change.",
      "oracle_id": "bd0c0e85-ff24-46c9-a547-4f633355c131",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells and abilities that cause players to gain life still resolve while Giant Cindermaw is on the battlefield. No player will gain life, but any other effects of that spell or ability will happen.",
      "oracle_id": "bd0c0e85-ff24-46c9-a547-4f633355c131",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells and abilities that replace or redirect damage are not affected by this card.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"damage can't be prevented\" statement overrides all forms of preventing damage. Damage prevention spells and abilities can still be cast and activated, they just don't do anything.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Deflecting Palm doesn't target any permanent or player. You choose a source of damage as Deflecting Palm resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "dc5dffc8-fac5-4956-bac4-1ad2cc16f6be",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If multiple prevention and/or replacement effects are trying to apply to the same damage, the player who would be dealt damage chooses the order in which to apply them.",
      "oracle_id": "dc5dffc8-fac5-4956-bac4-1ad2cc16f6be",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
